NAME
     vecprobe - does a task's vector register file survive a system call?

SYNOPSIS
     vecprobe

DESCRIPTION
     vecprobe loads the vector registers with known values, makes a
     system call (a printf) and sums them again. It says whether the
     registers came back intact. On this kernel they do; the same probe
     on Linux shows the registers discarded on every system call, which
     Linux does by design.

SEE ALSO
     vhold(1), memck(1)
